{%- set slug = theme.repository | replace(from="https://github.com/", to="") -%}
{%- set owner = slug | split(pat="/") | first -%}
{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
{%- set mirror = theme.id ~ "-zsh" -%}
# {{ theme.name }} zsh-syntax-highlighting Theme

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This repository is a read-only mirror.
> Issues, pull requests, and stars should go to [{{ slug }}]({{ theme.repository }}).

zsh-syntax-highlighting themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Requirements

- [zsh-syntax-highlighting](https://github.com/zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting)

> [!WARNING]
> This theme must be loaded **after** zsh-syntax-highlighting.
> The theme works by overriding `ZSH_HIGHLIGHT_STYLES` variables set by zsh-syntax-highlighting.

## Installation

### Manual

Clone the repository and source the theme file in your `.zshrc`:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}.git
source /path/to/{{ mirror }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.zsh
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ mirror }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.zsh
```
{% endfor %}
### zinit

```zsh
zinit light-mode for \
  pick"{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.zsh" \
  {{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```zsh
zinit light-mode for \
  pick"{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.zsh" \
  {{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}
```
{% endfor %}
### sheldon

Add to your `~/.config/sheldon/plugins.toml`:

```toml
[plugins.{{ mirror }}]
github = "{{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}"
use = ["{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.zsh"]
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```toml
[plugins.{{ mirror }}]
github = "{{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}"
use = ["{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.zsh"]
```
{% endfor %}
### oh-my-zsh

Clone as a custom plugin:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ owner }}/{{ mirror }} ${ZSH_CUSTOM:-~/.oh-my-zsh/custom}/plugins/{{ mirror }}
```

Then add to your `.zshrc`:

```zsh
plugins=(... {{ mirror }})
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
To use {{ v.variant.id }} variant, set before loading oh-my-zsh:

```zsh
export {{ theme.id | upper }}_VARIANT={{ v.variant.id }}
```
{% endfor %}
### antigen

```zsh
antigen bundle {{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
To use {{ v.variant.id }} variant, set before loading:

```zsh
export {{ theme.id | upper }}_VARIANT={{ v.variant.id }}
```
{% endfor %}
